    <page id="Info" tabgroup="pages" tabpage="10" style="left: 422dp; top: 96dp; width: 1342dp; height: 832dp">
        <img src="Page-Info.png" />
        <text id="Changelog" class="Changelog" style="left: 36dp; top: 92dp; width: 1270dp; height: 348dp">
            Ostirus Update 02.09.2026<br />

            <!--            <br />"INFO":<br />-->

            <!--            <br />"INFO" page now includes "Changelog" section that lists all updates made to latest version of skin.<br />-->

            <br />"PART-MANAGER":<br />

            <br />"Load-Preset" and "Save-Preset" buttons in "Part-Manager" have been fixed — they now work correctly in both "Single-Mode" and "Multi-Mode".
            "Multi-Mode" toggle button has been replaced with less bright version. "Snow" skin has been removed, as it is no longer needed. When switching "ROM" modes,
            skin now automatically adapts to selected "ROM" and updates "Part Manager" image accordingly.<br />

            <br />"OSCILLATOR":<br />

            <br />On "Oscillator" page in "Classic" mode, waveform morphing visualization has been added. When adjusting "Oscillator 1/2 Waveform Shape" parameter,
            displayed waveform now smoothly morphs between two selected types. Morphing also works between "Saw" and "Pulse" modes and responds to changes in "Pulsewidth" parameter.
            In "Hypersaw" mode, voices state display has been fixed — visualization now updates correctly when adjusting "Density" and "Detune" parameters.<br />

            <br />"FILTER":<br />

            <br />"Filter" page now features fully functional "ADSR" model for all envelope types. Parameters can be adjusted either via knobs or by dragging small square markers directly on
            "ADSR" graph. These markers move in different directions depending on which parameter they control. "Decay" square marker is particularly versatile — dragging it horizontally
            changes "Decay" parameter, while dragging vertically changes "Sustain" parameter.<br />
            Simultaneous control of "Cutoff" and "Resonance" parameters has been implemented via dedicated square markers located on LCD display of "Filter Cutoff" knob.
            Main screen shows values of both parameters at same time.<br />
            Double-clicking square markers resets "Resonance" parameter, while double-clicking elsewhere on LCD display resets "Cutoff" parameter. Same reset behavior applies to squares
            markers in "ADSR" area. Parameters can also be adjusted using mouse wheel, with adjustment speed controlled by "CTRL", "SHIFT", and "ALT" modifier keys — exactly as implemented in
            plugin for native knobs, both in drag mode and when using mouse wheel.<br />
            In "ADSR" area, solid color fill without gradient is used, and lines are drawn with slight angles, as current version lacks support for gradients and "Bezier curves".
            This will be improved once appropriate methods become available in "Canvas" toolkit.<br />
            "Analog Mode" button now remembers last value set by user within group, so state persists between last selected value in "Classic" (0–3) and "Analog" (4–7) groups.<br />

            <br />"LFO":<br />

            <br />On "LFO" page, behavior of "Clock Switch" button has been fixed. It now correctly toggles between "Rate" knob (which controls LFO speed in "Free" mode) and "Clock Divider"
            knob (tied to clock generator). Essentially, this button changes "LFO 1/2/3 Clock" values, mirroring behavior of dropdown menu responsible for same parameter.<br />

            <br />"ARPEGGIATOR":<br />

            <br />On arpeggiator page, you can now adjust "Length" and "Velocity" parameters by grabbing edge of visual "Step" and dragging vertically or horizontally, depending on
            which parameter you want to change. Adjustment speed is controlled by CTRL, SHIFT, and ALT modifier keys — similar to how it works with native knobs in plugin, both when dragging
            and when using mouse wheel.<br />
            You can also adjust both parameters simultaneously by dragging upper-right corner of "Step". With SHIFT held down, only "Length" parameter changes; with CTRL held down, only
            "Velocity" changes. ALT key slows down adjustment speed.<br />
            All draggable areas are marked in yellow and highlight on hover. Main display shows both parameter values simultaneously. Double-clicking corresponding areas resets parameters to
            their default values. Reset is also performed by double-clicking body of "Step" itself.<br />
            Mouse wheel works as well — scrolling normally changes "Velocity" parameter, while holding SHIFT changes "Length" instead.<br />
            Holding "ALT" key activates "Drawing" mode. Click anywhere to set "Velocity" of that step to your chosen value, or drag across entire arpeggiator area to paint custom pattern.
            Two additional drawing options are available: "ALT+SHIFT" lets you draw straight line at any angle from start point to end point (this mode only works when moving in original
            direction; moving backward falls back to regular drawing mode), and "ALT+SHIFT+CTRL" draws horizontal straight line, height of which is set by first click — then simply drag across
            arpeggiator area to achieve desired result.<br />
            You can also copy arpeggiator patterns — simply start editing any parameter by dragging edge of "Step", and that step will automatically be copied to "User-Pattern",
            where it can be edited further.<br />
            To copy "Step", middle-click it and drag to target "Step". Right-clicking toggles "Step" on or off ("Bitfield" parameter) — just click individual steps or drag across area.<br />
            "Slider" responsible for arpeggiator pattern length can now be interacted with not only by dragging but also by clicking on desired numbers within its area.<br />
            All parameter visualizations automatically adapt to global "Note Length" and "Swing" settings.<br />
            "Randomize Lengths", "Randomize Velocity", and "Randomize Step"(Minimum number of active steps is at least 25%) buttons have been added — each sets random values for active steps.<br />
            "Left" and "Right" buttons perform cyclic shift of steps in corresponding direction.<br />
            "Fill" button replicates current pattern across all thirty-two steps.<br />
            "Reset" button completely resets all parameters to their default values for all thirty-two steps.<br />

            <br />"FX-2":<br />

            <br />"Delay" and "Reverb" effect "Switches" have been left as they are, since they are native controls for effect states. Their behavior fully follows factory logic,
            and there is no need to create additional buttons or try to override their operation. Full functionality has not yet been implemented by developers, but this will be
            addressed in future update, at which point switches will work as expected.<br />
        </text>
